PROPOSAL (not applied): job results get a third outcome, "nothing to do", plus a weekly DOK job.

What it adds
  - roster-server/job-results.js: a code may carry `nothing: true` (ok stays true: nothing failed);
    stored result and /health jobs gain a `nothing` boolean. New PC codes nothing-no-pages,
    nothing-no-school (nothing) and reader-down (failed). New job weeklyDok: ok,
    nothing-below-floor, nothing-already-ran, failed.
  - status.html: a fresh nothing result is a new neutral blue "idle" tile (reason shown), order
    red > amber > idle > green, stale rule unchanged (36 h; 8 days for weeklyDok), new "Weekly DOK"
    tile (id weeklydok) with judgeWeeklyDok exported, rules <li> updated.
  - roster-server/tests/job-results.test.js and tests/status-page.test.js updated (tile count 8 -> 9).

Deploy notes
  - roster-server auto-deploys to Railway on push to master. Do NOT push during a live B or E class block.
  - tools/daily_pc_reconcile.ps1 already falls back to 'page-not-ready' when the server answers 400
    to a new code, so the PC reporter is safe before this deploys.
  - Weekly DOK reports fail harmlessly (logged) until this deploys; the Weekly DOK tile reads amber
    "unknown" until its first report afterwards.
  - status.html has no dark theme today, so only light-theme tokens (--st-idle, --st-idle-bg) were added.

Check: git apply --check tools/_proposals/job-result-three-state.patch   (lines before the first
"diff --git" are ignored by git apply)

